.TH "YAMLR-DIFF" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
Preview the changes the native healer would make to YAML manifests. The command does not modify files.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
yamlr diff [PATH] [-u|--unified]
.RE
.fi
\fBPATH\fR may be a YAML file or a directory. It defaults to the current directory. Directories are traversed recursively for \fB.yaml\fR and \fB.yml\fR files.
.PP
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-u\fR, \fB--unified\fR: Render changes in unified diff form. Without this option, show an inline word diff.
The target path and \fB-u\fR may appear in either order. Other options are currently unsupported and return a usage error; this command does not accept \fB--output-file\fR, \fB--exit-zero\fR, \fB--helm\fR, \fB--kustomize\fR, \fB--crd\fR, or Kubernetes-version flags.
.PP
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
yamlr diff
yamlr diff ./manifests
yamlr diff ./deployment.yaml --unified
yamlr diff --unified ./manifests
.RE
.fi
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR: The preview completed and no changes were proposed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB1\fR: At least one file has proposed changes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB3\fR: The target path does not exist.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB4\fR: A manifest could not be read or directory traversal failed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB3\fR: An unsupported option or extra target path was supplied.
